  "Missing hydrogens follow the force-field template of each residue (number of H per atom) with VSEPR geometry. Cut bonds get H caps (fixed X–H length).",
  "Ligands: one heavy-atom structure fixes the hydrogens and the charge. Every sp² carbon gets one double bond. The keto form is preferred. An sp² ring N without a double bond carries one H. P keeps one P=O bond. S keeps up to two S=O bonds. At pH 7, COOH, phosphate, phosphonate, sulfonate and sulfate groups lose their O–H hydrogen. Aliphatic amines stay neutral and are flagged, because most of them are protonated at pH 7. Tetrazoles and acyl sulfonamides stay neutral and are flagged, because most of them are anionic at pH 7. Hydrogens of the file stay only with a matching number. The PDB formula (FORMUL) checks the count. A MOL2 or PQR file with a pKa-based state (e.g. from Epik or PROPKA) is the recommended source of the ligand charge.",
